{"A":"Test a collision-safe hash-table lookup fast path: after computing the candidate hash, compare it with each bucket entry’s stored hash before calling `memcmp`. Keep the full key comparison whenever hashes match, so hash collisions cannot merge states. Leave BFS order and insertion semantics unchanged; measure this independently against baseline and validate exact outputs.","B":"Investigate the measured best candidate’s box-state changes: build a generation-stamped occupancy/index map once per expanded state, use it for constant-time box checks, and maintain the canonical sorted box vector with shifts and lower-bound reinsertion only on pushes. Keep strict bounds checks. Run ablations as well as the combination; validate stamp rollover, exact outputs, and performance rather than assuming the small observed gain is robust.","C":"Explore a serial duplicate-check-before-allocation path. Generate each legal successor’s canonical key in reusable scratch storage, hash and check it against the visited table, and allocate/copy a pooled state only when the key is new. Preserve collision-safe full-key equality, goal handling, parent links, direction/commit order, and BFS tie behavior. Compare with baseline and B’s candidate; do not pursue straightforward OpenMP frontier parallelism unless new measurements justify it.","G":"Integrate only correctness-validated tree programs. Start from baseline and the B occupancy/sorted-box/bounds candidate; then measure combinations with A and C independently and together, since gains may interact. Compare actual integrated timings and exact oracle outputs, retain only a measured correct improvement, and do not assume individually measured changes add. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.","analysis":"The task requires shortest Sokoban move sequences and correct tie selection, so preserve the reference BFS semantics and validate exact output, not just solvability. Baseline is reported correct on four cases at 0.004816 s. The B occupancy/sorted-box/bounds combination is the fastest reported candidate at 0.004764 s, about 1.1% lower; its hash variant is 0.004805 s. The A candidates are 0.004954 and 0.005012 s, and the C OpenMP candidates are 0.004877 and 0.004899 s. These are small differences, and candidate correctness is not reported in the observations; treat them as hypotheses and measure the integrated program rather than assuming additive gains."}